Ataree - eBPF-based Monitoring Tool
===================================

Overview
--------
Ataree loads a small eBPF program that hooks ptrace/openat/mmap/mprotect and sched fork/exit tracepoints, streams ringbuf events to userland, and runs lightweight Go detectors to raise alerts for process-injection behavior.

Current Features
----------------
- eBPF loader/attacher using cilium/ebpf (tracepoints: ptrace, openat, mmap, mprotect, sched fork/exit).
- Ring buffer reader -> RawEvent decoder -> detector fan-out -> stdout alerts.
- Graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

Detectors
---------
- ptrace-write: alert on PTRACE_POKETEXT/POKEDATA.
- ptrace-setregs: alert on PTRACE_SETREGS hijack attempts.
- ptrace->mprotect: correlate ptrace activity followed by mprotect(PROT_EXEC) within 5s.
- proc-maps-mem: correlate /proc/<pid>/maps then /proc/<pid>/mem within 5s.
- anon-exec-mmap: alert on MAP_ANONYMOUS | PROT_EXEC mappings.

Build & Run
-----------
- Build eBPF object: `make` (or use prebuilt under ebpf/).
- Build/runtime: `go build ./cmd/ataree` or run `./build/ataree`.

PoC Suite
---------
Process-injection PoCs live under `poc_malware/` (T1055 sub-techniques) for manual validation.

Docs
----
More detail in `docs/` and the site: https://hxuu.github.io/ataree/
